[Music]  this is your tech news briefing for  wednesday august 24th i'm zoe thomas for  the wall street journal  twitter is facing new allegations at a  sensitive time for the social media  business  the company's former head of security  peter zatko has filed a whistleblower  complaint with the securities and  exchange commission according to a  representative of whistleblower aid an  organization that helped file the claim  he accuses the company of failing to  protect sensitive user data and of lying  about its security problems  the accusations come just weeks before  twitter is set to face off against elon  musk in court over his attempt to back  out of a deal to buy the company  here to discuss the new allegations and  how they could affect twitter is our  tech reporter sarah needleman hey sarah  thanks for joining me it's great to be  here  so start by telling us a little bit more  about what this whistleblower is  alleging  sure um well there are many allegations  but broadly speaking he's alleging that  the company's been pretty laxed with its  security and privacy processes  but more specifically  the complaint goes into allegations that  the company has been  misrepresenting the number of  monetizable daily users on this platform  and that's the number it uses to  calculate spam  and fake accounts or estimate spam fake  accounts and that's interesting because  that is the main area focus for elon  musk who's in a legal battle with  twitter and he has argued that he should  be able to walk away from his 44 billion  dollar deal for the company because he  believes that it has been dishonest and  is actually committed fraud by not  providing um accurate numbers on that  issue so this complaint appears to sort  of support mr musk's theory so who  exactly is this whistleblower who's  making these allegations  uh this whistleblower was twitter's head  of security but he was uh fired from the  company in january  he has a long resume in the security  area he's worked for the us government  he's also worked for google and  for stripe the payments company  according to his linkedin he's also a  former hacker who is known as mudge and  he's been a noted computer security  researcher for decades  he was a member of a boston cyber  security collective they came to  prominence in 1998 when it offered  warnings about the state of national  cyber security and testimony to the  senate  and during one senate hearing the group  famously told the lawmakers they could  take down the internet in 30 minutes  so he was part of that collective so  that's just the point being that this is  um not just any cyber security  professional this is someone who's been  in the field for decades and is very  well known and he was brought on by jack  dorsey who at the time was still chief  executive of twitter to help it improve  its security and privacy policies  and practices but within about a year he  was fired and a twitter spokeswoman said  that he was fired for  ineffective leadership and poor  performance the spokeswoman also said  that the complaint is riddled with  inconsistencies and inaccuracies and  lacks important context  so we know zadko was hired by former  chief executive and co-founder jack  dorsey but what was his relationship  with the current ceo parag agarwal  what we know from the complaint is that  mr zacco has accused mr agrawal of being  dishonest with the board um he has  accused mr agrawal of pressuring him to  essentially report false or misleading  information to the board  and has agarwal at all responded to  these accusations  well mr agro put out a memo to employees  on tuesday and that was shared on  twitter of course  he said he knows it's frustrating  confusing for employees to read uh this  complaint  which he called inaccurate and he  defended twitter's work on privacy and  security  and he added that the you know attention  that the complaint has brought to the  company is going to make it harder for  them to do their jobs uh mr agwal also  said that the company is going to pursue  all paths to defend its integrity  as a company and set the record straight  so you mentioned that this complaint  appears to support musk's theory on the  number of bots on the platform have we  heard anything from musk or his team on  this  a lawyer for mr musk said that they've  already subpoenaed mr zacco  and that they found his exit from the  company and and that of other employees  curious  in light of what they've been finding  through the discovery process  what do we know about how this complaint  came about in the first place sure he  joined the company in late 2020 and  sometime over the course of 2021 he  started raising concerns  about the company's security and privacy  policies  and essentially he said in the complaint  that those were swept under the rug and  that he was actually discouraged from  bringing the concerns he had to the  board  and so he ultimately was fired in  january and in early march he went ahead  and approached the whistleblower  organization which resulted in the  complaint that was filed in july and  that has become public  so what comes next here what comes next  for the whistleblower and what comes  next for twitter  well for the whistleblower it's going to  be a matter of whether or not the  federal agencies are going to launch an  investigation so the department of  justice for example the sec  they've all been made aware of the  complaint when it was filed and so the  question is whether or not they're going  to  launch investigations into the matter  for twitter again it depends on whether  or not the federal agencies launched an  investigation in which case it would be  expected to  deal with that the company right now is  preparing for its lawsuit  against mr musk there's a five-day trial  scheduled to begin uh in october  that's a non-jury trial and so the  company right now is preparing for that  all right that was our reporter sarah  needleman thanks so much for joining us  sarah my pleasure  and that's it for tech news briefing  today  you know if you enjoy the show why not  tell a friend about it or leave us a  five star rating and a review it helps  others find the show and it lets us know  you like what we're doing i'm zoe thomas  for the wall street journal thanks for  listening  [Music]  you

